{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>No longer, etc.</b> This verse indicates that for Zion's sake is the word of HaShem, and he said: 'I will not be silent' — in the language of human beings." "<b>My delight is in her.</b> Two words." "<b>Be married. [Behold,] interpret it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {2 "Bracketed text [הנה] likely supplied by editor; translated literally. The comment is extremely terse: Ibn Ezra directs the reader to interpret the form, i.e., parse its grammar."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:39.355651964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}